! H2O | Standalone water at wB97X-D/6-31G(d,p)/PCM(water)
!
! Part of the standalone hydration thermodynamic cycle:
!   dG_hydration = G(hydrate) - [G(aldehyde) + G(water)]
! This supplies G(water), needed to balance the reactant side of the
! equation (the hydrate has one more O and two more H than the bare
! aldehyde). A single water molecule embedded in a PCM continuum is a
! standard, if approximate, way to estimate water's chemical potential --
! it does not fully capture bulk liquid water's extensive hydrogen-bonded
! structure, but is a reasonable and widely-used approximation, and will be
! applied consistently across both the acetaldehyde calibration and the
! chloroacetaldehyde case.
!
! Starting geometry: one of the two spectator water molecules extracted
! from the converged "first" IRC-point cluster geometry, purely as a
! reasonable starting guess (a lone water molecule's own geometry is not
! sensitive to which cluster it happened to come from; it will fully relax
! on optimization regardless).
!
! Settings identical to caa008-aldehyde-bare.inp/caa008-hydrate-bare.inp.

 $CONTRL SCFTYP=RHF RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE DFTTYP=wB97X-D
         COORD=UNIQUE MAXIT=200 NOSYM=1
 $END
 $GUESS GUESS=HUCKEL $END
 $BASIS GBASIS=N31 NGAUSS=6 NDFUNC=1 NPFUNC=1 $END
 $SCF CONV=1.0D-6
     SOSCF=.T.
     DAMP=.F.
     SHIFT=.T.
     DIRSCF=.TRUE.
 $END
 $STATPT OPTTOL=0.0001 NSTEP=300 IHREP=1 HSSEND=.T. DXMAX=0.02 NPRT=1 $END
 $ZMAT DLC=.F. AUTO=.F. $END
 $FORCE METHOD=SEMINUM PROJCT=.T. $END
 $PCM SOLVNT=WATER $END
 $SYSTEM MWORDS=20 MEMDDI=50 $END

 $DATA
Water, standalone, for hydration thermodynamic cycle
C1
O     8.0      3.9842881842     2.6765444468    -4.8076254061
H     1.0      3.5078817045     2.7937321447    -5.6358114425
H     1.0      3.3874282656     3.0329158850    -4.1299822164
 $END
